{"message":"I double-checked the available personal-card documentation. It lists APY bonuses for the Bronze Rewards, Silver Rewards, Gold Rewards, Platinum Rewards, Diamond Elite, EcoCard, Green Rewards, and Crypto-Cash Back cards, but it does not document travel-insurance coverage for any of them. The only card with explicitly documented travel insurance is the Business Platinum Rewards Card, which you correctly noted is not suitable for your personal needs.

Therefore, I can’t responsibly identify a personal credit card that meets your travel-insurance requirement, and I won’t recommend one based only on its APY bonus. Among the checking/savings combinations documented so far, Green Account + Gold Account still provides the highest documented savings yield: 5.5% base APY plus Green’s +0.75% boost, with Green offering direct deposit up to one day early. An EcoCard could add a documented +0.6% Gold savings bonus, but its travel-insurance coverage is not documented.

The travel-friendly Purple Account includes travel insurance as a checking-account benefit and provides direct deposit up to two days early, but its Gold savings boost is only +0.1%. I have not opened or closed any accounts. I can proceed with a combination once a personal card with documented travel insurance is identified or you decide that the checking-account travel insurance is sufficient."}
